fix(ui): F-0019 regression - status words fit the Sensors column

Finding:     regression named by the round-1 fix review (run 20261007-102219-fix-review)
             against F-0019.patch: the new status words did not fit the narrow Sensors
             column. At 320 px "Warning" was clipped to "Warnin"; at 1024-1440 px
             "Warning"/"Alarm" dropped to a second line, away from their dot.
Originating: at 320-1440 px every status word is fully visible without scrolling the
             table; from 360 px up the dot and word share one line.
Regression:  full `uie audit` (22 checks); journey switch-dosing-to-manual; diff vs
             baseline: 0 introduced findings or instances.
Drift class: local defect -> th/td horizontal padding 7px -> 4px (also onto the 4 px
             spacing scale), and the Status cell kept on one line from 360 px up.
Layer:       index.html (class="status" on the 5 Status cells), styles.css (th/td
             padding, .status rule in a min-width: 360px query).
Assumptions: none.
Left alone:  at 320 px the word sits under its dot (fully readable; cosmetic, in the
             debt register).
Re-test:     run 20261007-102909-fix-f-0019-regression: all gate checks except the
             pre-existing deferred census/motion/tells items at 0; journey 3/3;
             captures at 320/375/1024/1280 show full words. PASSED.
Baseline:    665ca185ac74f08453715a82013e960438c2e377; apply after F-0003, F-0021,
             F-0019.

